        "original_id": "cb945557-3c4a-55d0-b0f9-461d4bf9c9e2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Raymond Scott\n- Products: Clavivox\n- Topics: electronic instrument invention, music technology\n\nFacts:\n- Raymond Scott, born Harry Warnow, was born on September 10, 1908, and died on February 8, 1994.\n- Raymond Scott was an American composer, band leader, pianist, engineer, recording studio maverick, and electronic instrument inventor.\n- Raymond Scott invented the Clavivox in 1952.\n- The Clavivox was a keyboard sound synthesizer and sequencer.\n- The Clavivox was patented in 1956.",
